-------------------------------------------------
Deployment 
create deployment.yaml file  

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: productapi-deployment
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: productapi
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: productapi
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: productapi
        image: productapi:v1
        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8080
------------------------------------
create service and expose API
service.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: productapi-service
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: productapi
  ports:
    - port: 8080
      targetPort: 8080
      nodePort: 30080
------------------------------
Deploy to Kubernetes 

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
kubectl apply -f service.yaml

Check deployment
kubectl get pods

You should see something like:

productapi-deployment-xxxx   Running

Check service:

kubectl get svc
--------------------

Access your API

Get Minikube URL:

minikube service productapi-service

OR manually:

http://localhost:30080

Swagger:

http://localhost:30080/swagger
---------------------

Debug commands (VERY important)

If something fails:

Pods status
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>
Logs
kubectl logs -l app=productapi
